WEBVTT

00:01:00.369 --> 00:01:01.849
Good evening everyone.

00:01:02.169 --> 00:01:06.900
It is 5:30 on Thursday, August 27th, 2026,

00:01:07.169 --> 00:01:12.129
and this meeting of the Huntsville City Council is called to order.

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:15.449
Welcome to everyone who has joined us in the chambers or who is joining

00:01:15.449 --> 00:01:16.389
us remotely.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:19.519
All members of the council are present.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:24.319
We will begin, as is our practice, with an invocation offered by one of

00:01:24.319 --> 00:01:27.500
our, uh, Huntsville, Alabama public safety chaplains.

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:30.959
Tonight we have Rachel Harper with us, and that will be followed by the

00:01:30.959 --> 00:01:34.239
Pledge of Allegiance offered by council member John Meredith.

00:01:34.319 --> 00:01:37.040
All those who wish to and are able to do so,

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:39.639
please stand for the invocation and the pledge.

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:48.980
Father, we come to you tonight as a grateful people for all the many blessings

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:54.459
that you have afforded us and for the opportunity that we have each and

00:01:54.459 --> 00:01:57.480
every day to live in such a great nation.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:01.860
Father, I'm thankful for our leaders and for their hearts to serve,

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:02.540
Lord and.

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:07.459
I ask Father that we never ever take lightly the responsibilities that we

00:02:07.459 --> 00:02:08.820
have as servant leaders.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:13.940
I pray for continued blessings over our city and for wisdom,

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:17.619
Lord, over our city council in decisions made tonight.

00:02:17.979 --> 00:02:21.179
Lord, we pray for safety for all the men and women.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:27.279
Who, who give their lives, their lives on the line every day for your service

00:02:27.419 --> 00:02:28.850
and the protection of us.

00:02:29.179 --> 00:02:32.509
Lord, we just ask all these things in your precious name.

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:33.380
Amen.

00:02:38.789 --> 00:02:44.389
To the flag of the United States of America and to the republic for which

00:02:44.389 --> 00:02:50.449
it stands, one nation under God, indivisible with liberty and justice.

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:56.889
Thank you, Chaplain Harper.

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:57.589
Thank you, Mr.

00:02:57.649 --> 00:02:58.149
Meredith.

00:02:58.979 --> 00:03:02.229
Council members, you have the agenda before you.

00:03:02.389 --> 00:03:05.940
Please note that item 8A will require executive session.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:09.380
Are there any changes or additions to be made to the agenda?

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:12.970
Hearing none of the agenda will be approved.

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:17.520
Uh, you also have, um, the minutes of the regular meeting of the city council

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.839
held on August 13, 2026.

00:03:19.919 --> 00:03:23.220
Are there any additions or changes to be made to those minutes?

00:03:24.389 --> 00:03:27.169
Seeing none, the minutes will stand approved.

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:29.190
We have two recognitions tonight.

00:03:29.389 --> 00:03:34.710
6A is a presentation recognizing the 65 year legacy of Big Ed's Pizza,

00:03:34.869 --> 00:03:35.289
and Mr.

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:37.690
Little, I believe you will be making that presentation.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:40.690
Oh.

00:03:46.149 --> 00:03:47.850
Our friends from Big Ed's here.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:54.220
Pizza It doesn't right there.

00:03:54.259 --> 00:03:56.009
All right, come on down, sir.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:06.410
And I'm sorry I didn't bring you guys any food.

00:04:06.649 --> 00:04:10.089
Yeah, yeah, if he didn't hear, he said he didn't bring us any pizza,

00:04:10.210 --> 00:04:12.509
so we're going to go ahead and vote this out when I leave here.

00:04:13.399 --> 00:04:14.039
So that's OK.

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:14.960
We'll swing by.

00:04:15.009 --> 00:04:15.330
Thank you.

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:17.630
I'd like to change my vote to a nay.

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:23.720
If he didn't bring us food, then I'm changing my vote tona.

00:04:24.959 --> 00:04:27.899
Well, Mayor Battle didn't bring me Britlin's either,

00:04:28.239 --> 00:04:29.640
so just saying.

00:04:29.799 --> 00:04:33.589
So yes, well, that's, that's, uh, holding on to a grudge if you're bringing

00:04:33.589 --> 00:04:34.399
back Britlin's.

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:36.160
That's when we used to eat there, yeah.

00:04:36.279 --> 00:04:36.839
Oh yeah.

00:04:37.239 --> 00:04:39.959
Well, I'm sure everybody that's lived in Huntsville for any amount of time

00:04:39.959 --> 00:04:44.160
has heard of Big Ed's Pizza celebrating 65 years of business in Huntsville,

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:46.200
which is quite a testament to good pizza.

00:04:46.489 --> 00:04:52.570
Um, I did a little, um, uh, research, and I can only find about 5 or 6 businesses

00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:55.250
that are still around as long as Big Ed's.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:56.190
So that's really great.

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:58.589
And this is a certificate recognizing that great,

00:04:58.890 --> 00:05:02.089
uh, the outstanding food and tradition and community service and it's signed

00:05:02.089 --> 00:05:04.890
by everybody on the council and the mayor too.

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:06.679
Yeah, so congratulations.

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:08.570
Yeah, yeah.

00:05:40.869 --> 00:05:42.170
Congratulations.

00:05:43.799 --> 00:05:48.480
6B is a presentation recognizing the dedicated volunteers of the Chaffee

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:52.440
community, and it is my honor to make that presentation representing the

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:54.239
Chaffee community tonight we have Mr.

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:55.140
Lyle Boyles and Mr.

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:55.760
Bill Gould.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:56.160
Mr.

00:05:56.279 --> 00:05:56.959
Boyles, Mr.

00:05:57.089 --> 00:05:58.480
Gould, will you come up please?

00:06:11.279 --> 00:06:13.140
Well, you, you stay there and I'll stand up.

00:06:13.779 --> 00:06:15.200
That's, that feels right.

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:16.059
That feels right.

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:23.779
If you didn't know, the Chaffee community has the one of the oldest and

00:06:23.779 --> 00:06:28.119
largest civic associations in the community.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:31.320
They are a neighborhood that is well connected.

00:06:31.339 --> 00:06:33.540
They are a neighborhood that really cares about their community.

00:06:33.695 --> 00:06:38.075
Community and tonight we're honoring them particularly for the unique service

00:06:38.244 --> 00:06:44.605
that they provide to caring for Logan Park in collaboration with Parks and

00:06:44.605 --> 00:06:45.375
Recreation.

00:06:45.734 --> 00:06:46.364
So Mr.

00:06:46.375 --> 00:06:48.524
Gould, would you share with us what it is you do?

00:06:48.855 --> 00:06:52.614
Sure, so, uh, starting in 2011.

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:56.350
The CNCA, the Chaffee Neighborhood Civic Association,

00:06:56.429 --> 00:06:59.510
reached an agreement with the city to take responsibility for opening and

00:06:59.510 --> 00:07:02.190
closing and basically tending to the park,

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:05.380
keeping an eye on things, letting them know our problems and issues,

00:07:06.109 --> 00:07:08.709
calling in when somebody was in there when they shouldn't be,

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:10.250
and activities going on.

00:07:10.869 --> 00:07:14.220
Lyle here was one of that first group.

00:07:14.429 --> 00:07:17.750
He was the actual founding member of it, and he's still in the rotation

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:18.079
today.

00:07:18.549 --> 00:07:19.910
Every once in a while he forgets his key,

00:07:19.950 --> 00:07:21.190
we've got to get it for him, but.

00:07:21.910 --> 00:07:23.950
But a group of 6 teams.

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:27.179
Every week, every 6 weeks you get a rotation,

00:07:27.260 --> 00:07:30.410
you take that week with a partner and somebody opens it in the morning,

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:33.730
opens the restrooms, checks the facilities to make sure that it's good,

00:07:34.059 --> 00:07:36.209
and then somebody else or that same team.

00:07:36.339 --> 00:07:37.579
Lyle does it by himself.

00:07:37.739 --> 00:07:40.959
He can't find a good partner, I guess, uh,

00:07:41.059 --> 00:07:45.100
we close it up every night when we see something we reach out so the.

00:07:45.350 --> 00:07:48.519
The partnership with the parks department is amazing.

00:07:48.709 --> 00:07:49.790
We are truly partners.

00:07:49.839 --> 00:07:51.309
If we need something, we just reach out.

00:07:51.429 --> 00:07:53.899
David Delier is my favorite pen pal.

00:07:54.149 --> 00:07:58.269
I send him a note saying there's a toilet that's running or there's a trash

00:07:58.269 --> 00:08:00.149
can that somebody took home as a souvenir,

00:08:00.230 --> 00:08:02.109
and the next day it's done, it's fixed.

00:08:02.959 --> 00:08:05.399
When we have issues, we can reach out to the police.

00:08:05.559 --> 00:08:08.920
We had somebody who was living in the keeping their car living in the park

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:10.739
while they were visiting their girlfriend down the street.

00:08:11.619 --> 00:08:14.500
The police department came over and helped us to clean that up.

00:08:14.739 --> 00:08:17.600
We've been doing that now for 15 years.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:22.220
We plan on doing it for a bit longer and we greatly appreciate the partnership

00:08:22.220 --> 00:08:27.700
and the support that allows us to keep our precious little park safe and

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:31.040
clean and a great place for the families to spend time,

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:32.099
so thank you.

00:08:32.599 --> 00:08:36.440
And I have 10 certificates here that I hope you will share with with all

00:08:36.440 --> 00:08:37.380
the folks who are involved.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:42.280
Yeah, if I could, those, those people are most of them still getting out

00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:45.799
of work when we're starting this, so it's not a bunch of retirees that just

00:08:45.799 --> 00:08:48.239
hang around and that's nothing to do but open and close the park.

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:50.400
They fit it in amongst everything else.

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:52.400
First thing in the morning, last thing at night,

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:54.299
we make sure that it's taken care of.

00:08:54.919 --> 00:08:58.369
And Lyle, we were talking before the meeting started about why this is so

00:08:58.369 --> 00:09:00.929
important and so do you want to comment on that?

00:09:01.210 --> 00:09:03.710
You don't just take care of the park just to make it look nice.

00:09:03.929 --> 00:09:06.570
Well, it's significant in the fact that the park was really.

00:09:06.849 --> 00:09:10.169
Uh, it's, it's secluded off of the South Memorial Parkway.

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:11.130
It was dark.

00:09:11.489 --> 00:09:13.330
There was a lot of nonsense going on in the park,

00:09:13.409 --> 00:09:16.409
vandalism, things of that nature, and as a result of doing this now for

00:09:16.409 --> 00:09:19.330
these years, that significantly reduced all of that.

00:09:19.409 --> 00:09:22.969
And again, we're so grateful to the city for the support we get from several

00:09:22.969 --> 00:09:25.190
of the departments, not just Parks and recreations,

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:27.190
but General Services and others are in there,

00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:29.950
and we do appreciate that and thank the city for that.

00:09:30.679 --> 00:09:34.640
And we're sharing this tonight not just because we want to recognize volunteers

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:37.239
and again here are the certificates we hope you'll share that,

00:09:37.429 --> 00:09:42.400
but this is a model we hope other communities can use so thank you both

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:45.950
for your service thank you to all the volun the Chaffee volunteers and for

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:46.940
the work that they do.

00:10:20.479 --> 00:10:22.239
