01:10:13.580 --> 01:10:14.319
Following Ms.

01:10:14.430 --> 01:10:16.149
Minsk, we will hear from Jerry Burnett.

01:10:30.520 --> 01:10:34.259
Hi, my name is Maggie Minsk, and I live in Madison,

01:10:34.879 --> 01:10:40.410
um, but I'm also a business owner, uh, in Huntsville's District 5.

01:10:41.180 --> 01:10:44.490
Um, I am a single mother and business owner,

01:10:44.569 --> 01:10:48.000
and I am also concerned about flock safety,

01:10:48.459 --> 01:10:51.490
um, which I believe is rather Orwellian, uh,

01:10:51.620 --> 01:10:55.640
in speech and might be more aptly named flock surveillance.

01:10:55.740 --> 01:10:57.569
I, I am truly concerned.

01:10:58.140 --> 01:11:02.000
Uh, the cameras take videos, essentially a warrantless search of everyone

01:11:02.220 --> 01:11:04.729
in Hunts, uh, Huntsville, Madison, Decatur,

01:11:04.810 --> 01:11:05.180
etc.

01:11:05.339 --> 01:11:07.000
all have contracts with flock.

01:11:07.410 --> 01:11:09.250
Um, Huntsville did it first.

01:11:09.410 --> 01:11:14.000
Madison got theirs, um, not too long ago for 86,000.

01:11:14.509 --> 01:11:18.729
Uh, the North Alabama Multi-agency Crime Center uses license plate readers,

01:11:18.890 --> 01:11:22.250
cameras, gunshot detection, which is microphones,

01:11:22.330 --> 01:11:24.729
and also intelligence AI.

01:11:25.160 --> 01:11:29.450
Um, however, statistically, it seems like a study of flat cameras showed

01:11:29.450 --> 01:11:34.169
that ALPRs, um, are wrong 71% of the time,

01:11:34.540 --> 01:11:36.890
leaving us to pay for a lawyer, take off work,

01:11:36.930 --> 01:11:39.479
and prove in court that it wasn't us.

01:11:39.950 --> 01:11:44.540
Um, so there's a concern about innocent until proven guilty,

01:11:44.609 --> 01:11:48.080
and once the data exists about all Huntsville citizens,

01:11:48.129 --> 01:11:50.109
it becomes a cybersecurity target.

01:11:50.910 --> 01:11:54.959
Uh, in January, Flock confirmed a security incident involving its Condor

01:11:54.959 --> 01:11:59.759
cameras that exposed live camera feeds and archival footage and allowed

01:11:59.759 --> 01:12:01.120
video to be deleted.

01:12:01.479 --> 01:12:06.160
Researchers have also demonstrated vulnerabilities in ALPR technology that

01:12:06.160 --> 01:12:09.419
exposed these surveillance systems to unauthorized access.

01:12:09.709 --> 01:12:13.140
Anything connected to a network is potentially vulnerable.

01:12:13.750 --> 01:12:16.600
Two days ago, uh, August 25th, Pflugerville,

01:12:16.720 --> 01:12:20.680
Texas unanimously voted to end its flock contract after it was revealed

01:12:20.680 --> 01:12:29.970
that 1.6 million searches had been conducted by 459 outside organizations

01:12:30.450 --> 01:12:32.100
within a six month period.

01:12:33.200 --> 01:12:37.569
This week, a US Senate Judiciary Subcommittee opened a formal investigation

01:12:37.569 --> 01:12:40.879
into FL's data collection, access, and sharing practices.

01:12:41.189 --> 01:12:45.259
Fox's own materials acknowledged that its LPR system is connected across

01:12:45.259 --> 01:12:50.799
49 states, while the ALC ACLU has raised concern about the creation of a

01:12:50.799 --> 01:12:53.819
nationwide surveillance infrastructure.

01:12:54.330 --> 01:12:58.339
As a mental health professional, I'm concerned about the privacy and safety

01:12:58.339 --> 01:13:01.839
