01:25:11.529 --> 01:25:12.609
Good evening everyone.

01:25:12.910 --> 01:25:16.830
I'm here tonight to demand rejection of the expansion of automatic license

01:25:16.830 --> 01:25:18.290
plate reader surveillance.

01:25:18.750 --> 01:25:21.910
This is often presented as a simple public safety tool,

01:25:22.029 --> 01:25:25.830
but that description leaves out the most important question what happens

01:25:25.830 --> 01:25:29.910
to the relationship between citizens and government when the government

01:25:29.910 --> 01:25:33.669
is allowed to collect information on everyone all the time without suspicion

01:25:33.669 --> 01:25:34.430
of wrongdoing?

01:25:35.200 --> 01:25:39.399
ALPRs collect license plates, locations, and time stamps from everyone who

01:25:39.399 --> 01:25:41.259
happens to drive past a camera.

01:25:41.799 --> 01:25:44.959
That means the government can build a searchable record of where ordinary

01:25:44.959 --> 01:25:48.479
people have been, even when those people are not suspected of committing

01:25:48.479 --> 01:25:49.180
any crime.

01:25:50.109 --> 01:25:53.419
That is an inversion of a basic principle of a free society.

01:25:54.160 --> 01:25:57.640
We are being asked to accept a system where everyone is treated as a potential

01:25:57.640 --> 01:25:58.740
future suspect.

01:25:59.240 --> 01:26:02.220
The government collects first and justifies the search later.

01:26:02.660 --> 01:26:04.899
Instead of public power being limited and accountable,

01:26:05.279 --> 01:26:08.379
ordinary people are made permanently available for inspection.

01:26:08.830 --> 01:26:12.160
Citizens should not have to live under constant surveillance so that someday

01:26:12.160 --> 01:26:15.399
the government might decide their past movements are worth investigating.

01:26:16.060 --> 01:26:18.569
And surveillance does not fall equally on everyone.

01:26:18.990 --> 01:26:22.109
People who work irregular hours, rely on older vehicles,

01:26:22.299 --> 01:26:25.109
travel across jurisdictions, organize with neighbors,

01:26:25.229 --> 01:26:29.870
attend protests, visit clinics, or move through heavily monitored areas

01:26:29.870 --> 01:26:32.450
are more likely to be recorded and scrutinized.

01:26:32.830 --> 01:26:35.979
A system that collects everyone's movements becomes a system that disciplines

01:26:35.979 --> 01:26:38.129
the people with the least power to challenge it.

01:26:38.709 --> 01:26:42.310
And once that infrastructure exists, the question is no longer simply whether

01:26:42.310 --> 01:26:43.850
we trust today's police department.

01:26:44.339 --> 01:26:47.250
It is whether we trust every future administration,

01:26:47.339 --> 01:26:51.220
every future employee with access, every agency this data may be shared

01:26:51.220 --> 01:26:53.859
with, and every future expansion of this technology.

01:26:54.680 --> 01:26:58.120
Power that can be abused finds someone willing to abuse it.

01:26:58.919 --> 01:27:02.109
We also need to ask whether the evidence justifies the cost.

01:27:02.520 --> 01:27:06.919
A quasi randomized study found an increase in vehicle recoveries but no

01:27:06.919 --> 01:27:10.020
increase in arrests and little clear evidence of general crime prevention

01:27:10.020 --> 01:27:10.720
benefits.

01:27:11.240 --> 01:27:14.879
Early experimental research into Northern Virginia jurisdictions found no

01:27:14.879 --> 01:27:16.979
statistically significant reduction in general crime,

01:27:17.169 --> 01:27:21.109
auto-related crime, auto theft, or theft from autos associated with ALPR

01:27:21.109 --> 01:27:21.950
patrols.

01:27:22.520 --> 01:27:25.399
Public resources should be directed towards measures that strengthen people's

01:27:25.399 --> 01:27:26.359
security directly.

01:27:26.740 --> 01:27:29.689
Reliable emergency response, housing stability,

01:27:29.859 --> 01:27:32.459
mental health services, safe transportation,

01:27:32.660 --> 01:27:35.029
and the conditions that allow people to live with dignity,

01:27:35.379 --> 01:27:38.620
a technology that expands the state's power to watch everyone should not

01:27:38.620 --> 01:27:41.649
take priority over investments that improve people's lives.

01:27:42.060 --> 01:27:45.540
A safe society does not require turning the entire public into a database

01:27:45.540 --> 01:27:48.359
just in case someone might be useful to an investigation later.

01:27:48.779 --> 01:27:52.859
